unicode_names comment:
'Unicode character names, GENERATED from the UCD.

DO NOT EDIT: regenerate with scripts/generate_unicode_names.py, which
documents why this exists.  In short, ``\N{NAME}'''' used to resolve
against a hand-curated table of 33 names kept in TWO places, and a name
outside it was a SyntaxError -- so one unremarkable literal,
``"\N{EMPTY SET}"'''', cost a whole 5300-line test module.

34137 names are stored here, plus 65 control ALIASES kept apart: a C0/C1
control has no name of its own, so without its alias it cannot be
reached by name at all.  The other 114716 that the UCD names are
ALGORITHMIC and computed instead: 11172 Hangul syllables composed from
jamo, and 103544 code points whose name is a fixed prefix plus their own
hex.  CPython does exactly this split, for the same reason -- storing
them would quadruple the table to say nothing new.

Unicode version: 16.0.0.'
%

expectvalue /Class
doit
unicode_names category: 'Grail-Modules'
%

